{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan corrected against the tree before review (rv9's two blocking findings plus four errors found by direct verification):\n\n1. Floor source #2 piped the ticket's nanosecond `created_at` straight into `git rev-list --before=`. Measured in this checkout: `--before=\"1787354756915214001\"` returns 960fbfef2f (the TIP of main), `--before=\"@1787354756\"` returns 767bb3ead6 (a real historical floor). The plan and the skill now spell out the `/ 1000000000` divide and the `@<unix-seconds>` form.\n2. Scope named `tests/unit/test_skill_frontmatter.py`, which does not exist; the real file is `tests/unit/test_check_skill_frontmatter.py`.\n3. `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/phases/` does not exist (the dir holds only SKILL.md, llm-behavioral-taxonomy.md, test-design.md), so it left Scope.\n4. `docs/user-guide.md` mentions neither rebar-debug nor agent-skills, so there was no sentence to amend; it left Scope and file_impact.\n5. The worktree mandate spans SKILL.md lines 40-52, not 40-43.\n6. The bug counts were wrong (221 claimed). Reproduced from `rebar list --type bug`: 764 total, 759 closed, 249 filed 7-21 Aug 2026. The closed majority is why Step 0's sweep is deliberately status-unfiltered - an open-only sweep sees 1 of 764 tickets.\n\nAlso corrected while writing the skill text: Step 0 mandates a `duplicates` link, which the file's own approval gate would have required user approval for, so the Step-0 link is added to the pre-approved carve-out list.\n\nreview-plan: PASS, certified at ed9beb1cb. Advisory T8 (no decision rule between 'link duplicates' and 'resume') was fixed in the skill text rather than argued: the choice is now decided by the match's status (open/in-progress -> resume in place; closed + behavior back -> regression, file and link; closed + never actually fixed -> reopen and resume).\n\nMutation evidence for tests/unit/test_rebar_debug_step0.py - 17 perturbations of the live SKILL.md, each killed a specific test and each restored: renaming the Step 0 heading; dropping 'fast path' from it; dropping the rebar list command; narrowing 'including closed tickets' to open; removing the Step-0 entry from the carve-out; changing the divisor to /1000 (both everywhere and in the command only); reintroducing --before=\"<created_at>\"; reintroducing 'rebar-version'; removing the unknown-version line; weakening 'reported on or after <sha>'; dropping the floor..origin/main log range; dropping the rebar link invocation; changing rev-parse origin/main to @{u}; and three perturbations of the new decision rule. An earlier partial divisor mutation SURVIVED because the assertion matched a prose occurrence, so the test was tightened to pin the divide inside the runnable command.\n\nGerrit change 2077."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787379093534172001,"uuid":"70dd75a5-fb36-4085-9227-d76fa9d2e808"}